Subject: [PATCH] gallium/tc: do not carry an ended renderpass into the next batch

If the call that ends a renderpass is the last one to fit in a batch, the
batch flush copies the ended info into the next batch and clears end_call.
The next draw makes the recording thread advance to a new info because the
info is marked ended. The driver thread only advances after executing
end_call, so it stays one info behind for the rest of that batch.

Each renderpass in that batch then sees the info of the one before it. In
Recoil, an MSAA RmlUi layer loses its resolve and the following pass to the
window-system framebuffer inherits it. The single-sampled BGRA framebuffer is
then resolved into the texture that pass is sampling, which shows blocks of
the image flipped with red and blue swapped.

Only copy the info when the ending call has not been recorded yet.
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c
@@ -280,6 +280,13 @@ tc_batch_increment_renderpass_info(struct threaded_context *tc, unsigned batch_idx, bool full_copy)
    batch->renderpass_info_idx++;
    tc_batch_renderpass_infos_resize(tc, batch);
    tc_info = batch->renderpass_infos.data;

+   /* the call that ended the renderpass is in the batch being flushed: nothing in the next batch
+    * continues that renderpass, and the driver only advances past an ended info at its end_call
+    */
+   if (full_copy && tc->renderpass_info_recording &&
+       tc_batch_rp_info(tc->renderpass_info_recording)->end_call)
+      full_copy = false;
+
    if (full_copy) {
       /* this should only be called when changing batches */
       assert(batch->renderpass_info_idx == 0);
